{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfmAqd5Loo7EcrVLNap2c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lighthouses have guided maritime navigation for centuries, standing as steadfast sentinels along treacherous coastlines. These iconic structures emit powerful beams that cut through fog, storm, and darkness, warning ships of rocky shores and hidden dangers. Built on isolated peninsulas, islands, and reefs, lighthouses require dedicated keepers who maintain the lights and navigation equipment. Modern lighthouses often operate automatically, yet they remain symbols of maritime heritage and human perseverance. Their rotating lights continue to save lives, making them enduring symbols of hope and safety at sea.\n\nNow let me run `ls` to see what's in the current directory."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9ec3688-ae21-44c1-92a8-26e665f24b71"}
